  "notes": "THE SOURCES NAME DIFFERENT PRODUCTIONS for the member after '->'. This is not a misspelling of one word as another: the two names are different words, and Tier B' made a judgement rather than fixing a character.\nReading A, the specification clause: 'ownedRelationship += InvocationTypeMember'. That name appears exactly once in the whole KerML wiki \u2014 this reference \u2014 and is defined nowhere, in KerML or SysML. Read literally the clause is incomplete here.\nReading B, Tier B': KerML-textual-bnf.kebnf:1136 puts 'InstantiatedTypeMember' in that slot. That production IS defined, at 8.2.5.8.3, and is what InvocationExpression and ConstructorExpression use for the same role. So the transcription substituted a defined production for an undefined one, silently.\nWhat makes B plausible: FunctionOperationExpression is typed ': InvocationExpression', so the slot is the type being invoked, which is exactly what InstantiatedTypeMember names elsewhere. What makes B a judgement rather than a repair: nothing in the specification says the two names denote the same thing, and 'invocation' and 'instantiated' are not variants of one word.\nThe Pilot Xtext has no rule under either name (0 occurrences of InvocationTypeMember in KerMLExpressions.xtext), so it offers no third opinion.\nNot resolved here. Taking Tier B' because it is the reading that compiles would be picking whichever is easier to implement, which .claude/rules/derivation.md forbids. For grammar-adjudicator."
